course: dictionary
lesson: 9923
title: Tangled: twisted or complicated
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer wants. «A real fox eats rabbits, mice, birds, worms, beetles, fruit and leftovers, so food chains join into a tangled food web, which lets animals switch food when one runs short.» A food web is not made of string, so tangled here does not mean knotted. The clues are web and join: many food chains are linked together in a messy, complicated way.
explain: Always test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try «a complicated food web, which lets animals switch food when one runs short». It still makes sense, so complicated is the right meaning here.
explain: The other meaning is twisted together in a messy way that is hard to undo, like tangled hair, tangled headphones or tangled wires. Ask yourself which meaning fits the words around it, and you will know which one to use.
fact: Tangle is the verb. Tangles, tangling and tangled are its other forms, and tangled is also an adjective.
fact: «Tangled» can mean twisted together in a messy way that is hard to undo, like hair, string or wires.
fact: «Tangled» can also mean complicated and confusing, like «a tangled food web».
fact: To get tangled up in something means to get caught in it or involved in it.
fact: Useful phrases to remember: «tangled up», «get tangled», and «a tangled mess».
exercise: «The fox lives in a tangled food web.» What does tangled mean here? | Very quiet | Torn into small pieces | Twisted into knots like wool | *Complicated and confusing, with many links
exercise: Mia says her hair is tangled after the windy walk. What does tangled mean? | Very short and cut | Neatly combed and shiny | *Twisted together in a messy way that is hard to brush out | Wet and cold
exercise: Which phrase means to get caught up in something? | Get older | Get a drink | *Get tangled up | Get dressed
test: In «a tangled story with many twists», what does tangled mean? | Short and simple | Wet through | Very funny | *Complicated and confusing
test: «The fishing line got tangled around the bird's feet.» What does tangled mean? | Lovely and bright | Left on the beach | Fast and quick | *Caught and twisted together, hard to undo
exam: Which sentence uses tangled to mean complicated and confusing? | The headphones were tangled in my bag | *The plot of the film was so tangled that I lost track of who was who | My tangled hair needs a good brush | The string was tangled in a ball on the floor
